# Reply pipeline walkthrough. Run 04-engine.http first so the contact received an email,
# then simulate their reply and work the review queue.
# Get an admin dev token first (02-auth.http) and paste it below.

@token = PASTE-AN-ADMIN-DEV-TOKEN
@contactId = PASTE-THE-CONTACT-ID

### Simulate a rate request from the contact (dev/staging only; runs the pipeline after commit)
# @name simulated
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-tools/sending-events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: simulate-rate-query-1

{"type": "reply", "contact_id": "{{contactId}}", "body": "Hi Maya, please quote 2x40HC from Chennai to Rotterdam, monthly, FOB."}

### What the pipeline did (idempotent: returns the stored result)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/replies/{{simulated.response.body.events[0].message_id}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Quote-ready lead for pricing
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pending review items
# @name reviews
GET {{baseUrl}}/ai/reviews?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One review item (draft, classification and context)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ai/reviews/{{reviews.response.body.items[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approve: sends the draft in the original thread (guardrails still apply)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/reviews/{{reviews.response.body.items[0].id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: approve-1

### ...or correct it first
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/reviews/{{reviews.response.body.items[0].id}}/edit-and-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: edit-approve-1

{"body": "Dear Ahmed,\n\nThank you. Our pricing team will send the quote today.\n\nMaya"}

### ...or reject it (nothing is sent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/reviews/{{reviews.response.body.items[0].id}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: reject-1

{"note": "Pricing will call instead."}

### The reply in the outbox (same thread as the intro)
GET {{baseUrl}}/outbox?contact_id={{contactId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Simulate a hard bounce (suppresses the contact, stops outreach)
POST {{baseUrl}}/test-tools/sending-events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: simulate-bounce-1

{"type": "bounce", "bounce_type": "hard", "contact_id": "{{contactId}}", "body": "550 5.1.1 user unknown"}

### Reply policy for every bucket
GET {{baseUrl}}/ai/reply-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Enable auto-send for interested replies (admin only; confident replies only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/ai/reply-policies/interested
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action_mode": "auto_send", "auto_send_enabled": true}

### Restore the default
PUT {{baseUrl}}/ai/reply-policies/interested
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Provider webhook (normally sent by the provider). The signature header is
### t=<unix>,v1=<hex hmac_sha256(secret, t + "." + body)>; compute it for the exact body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/sending/dry_run
Content-Type: application/json
X-LaneReach-Signature: t=0,v1=COMPUTE-ME

{"tenant_id": "PASTE-TENANT-ID", "events": [{"event_id": "evt-1", "type": "reply", "occurred_at": "2026-09-28T10:00:00+04:00", "from_email": "ahmed@gulf-importers.example", "body": "Tell me more"}]}
